From cf0e058b397555cbfbdb34cfa537778ac02a5168 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:52:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/62] Assemble: do not hold the container O_EXCL over
 start_mdmon()

mdmon_take_array() holds O_EXCL on the container over mdmon_running(),
start_mdmon() and the ping, so that a running mdmon cannot leave before
the ping has made it pick the new member array up.  An mdmon that
start_mdmon() starts needs no such guard: the array is started already,
and the first pass of its manager finds it.  Holding O_EXCL over
start_mdmon() costs time instead: if an mdmon@ came up meanwhile
(started by another program) and has not written its pid file yet,
mdmon_running() does not see it and start_mdmon() runs "systemctl
restart", which stops it.  That mdmon leaves on SIGTERM only with O_EXCL
on the container (wait_and_act()), which this mdadm holds: it waits for
open_dev_excl() to give up, and systemctl with it.

Drop O_EXCL when no mdmon runs, before start_mdmon().

IMSM containers on loop devices, and AMD RAIDXpert2 ones (later in this
series), a RAID1 in each, mdmon@ from the tree; the window is made wide
with an LD_PRELOAD that delays the start of mdmon by 3 s before its pid
file.  "systemctl start mdmon@", then mdadm -I of the container: without
the change -I takes 7.36-7.57 s (the restart waits 7.2 s for the first
mdmon to stop), with it 2.75-2.95 s - what is left of the 3 s.  Three
runs each.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 Assemble.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Assemble.c b/Assemble.c
index f81a418f..9ee95f17 100644
--- a/Assemble.c
+++ b/Assemble.c
@@ -1985,15 +1985,21 @@ free_st:
  * the ping misses it and the next member array of the same mdadm -I, not
  * seeing it run, starts it again - "systemctl restart", which stops the
  * one just started first.
+ * An mdmon started here needs no guard: it finds the array, already
+ * started, on its first pass.  Drop O_EXCL before start_mdmon(): should
+ * "systemctl restart" stop an mdmon that was coming up without its pid
+ * file yet, that one leaves on SIGTERM only with O_EXCL on the container.
  */
 static void mdmon_take_array(char *container_devnm)
 {
 	int fd = open_dev_excl(container_devnm);
 
-	if (!mdmon_running(container_devnm) &&
-	    start_mdmon(container_devnm) == 0 &&
-	    !check_env("MDADM_NO_MDMON"))
-		wait_for_mdmon_control_socket(container_devnm);
+	if (!mdmon_running(container_devnm)) {
+		close_fd(&fd);
+		if (start_mdmon(container_devnm) == 0 &&
+		    !check_env("MDADM_NO_MDMON"))
+			wait_for_mdmon_control_socket(container_devnm);
+	}
 	ping_monitor(container_devnm);
 	close_fd(&fd);
 }
